  "lyrics": [
    {
      "start": 0.05,
      "end": 1.736,
      "text": "Alright \u2014 picture this.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-01-0001s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 1.736,
      "end": 8.5,
      "text": "You\u2019re keeping track of fifty club members in a spreadsheet: names, emails, and phone numbers.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-01-0001s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.5,
      "end": 11.138,
      "text": "It feels simple enough\u2026 until it isn\u2019t.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-01-0001s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.138,
      "end": 12.944,
      "text": "Someone gets added twice.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-02-0010s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.944,
      "end": 15.555,
      "text": "Someone else\u2019s email gets overwritten.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-02-0010s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.555,
      "end": 23.152,
      "text": "Suddenly you\u2019re tracking payments, committees, and event RSVPs \u2014 and the whole thing turns into a mess.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-03-0015s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.152,
      "end": 26.75,
      "text": "That\u2019s the moment you realize you don\u2019t need a bigger spreadsheet.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-03-0015s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.75,
      "end": 33.43,
      "text": "You need structure: a better way to organize the data, connect it, and keep it from falling apart.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-03-0015s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.43,
      "end": 35.388,
      "text": "That\u2019s where databases come in.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-05-0033s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 35.388,
      "end": 37.305,
      "text": "So what is a database, really?",
      "slide": "slides/slide-05-0033s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.305,
      "end": 38.861,
      "text": "Why do we use tables?",
      "slide": "slides/slide-05-0033s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.861,
      "end": 40.43,
      "text": "What\u2019s a primary key?",
      "slide": "slides/slide-05-0033s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.43,
      "end": 48.43,
      "text": "And why does almost every app you use \u2014 social media, banking, you name it \u2014 run on something called an RDBMS?",
      "slide": "slides/slide-06-0040s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 48.48,
      "end": 49.916,
      "text": "Here's the short version.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-07-0047s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.916,
      "end": 55.485,
      "text": "A database organizes data with structure \u2014 tables, not one giant sheet.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-07-0047s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.485,
      "end": 59.777,
      "text": "Each table holds one kind of thing, in rows and columns.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-07-0047s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.777,
      "end": 65.638,
      "text": "A primary key uniquely identifies a row, so you can point at it and nowhere else.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-08-0057s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.638,
      "end": 69.402,
      "text": "An RDBMS is the software that stores that world.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-08-0057s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 69.402,
      "end": 71.332,
      "text": "SQL is how you talk to it.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-08-0057s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 71.398,
      "end": 75.009,
      "text": "And before we\u2019re done, you\u2019ll write your first line of SQL.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-08-0057s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 75.059,
      "end": 79.163,
      "text": "A relational database is a collection of related tables.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-08-0057s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 79.163,
      "end": 80.816,
      "text": "Not one giant sheet.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-08-0057s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 80.816,
      "end": 86.524,
      "text": "Separate tables, each with one job, that you connect when you need the whole story.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-08-0057s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 86.524,
      "end": 89.052,
      "text": "This diagram is a tiny store.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-08-0057s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 89.052,
      "end": 93.191,
      "text": "We'll add one table at a time, so you can actually see the pieces.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-08-0057s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 93.191,
      "end": 94.885,
      "text": "First: users.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-09-0091s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 94.885,
      "end": 96.885,
      "text": "These are the people with accounts.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-09-0091s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 96.885,
      "end": 102.024,
      "text": "Each row is one person \u2014 an email, an id, a password.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-09-0091s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 102.024,
      "end": 103.316,
      "text": "Hold that picture.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 103.316,
      "end": 104.816,
      "text": "Users is the hub.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 104.816,
      "end": 107.038,
      "text": "Other tables will point back here.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 107.038,
      "end": 108.33,
      "text": "Now products.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 108.33,
      "end": 111.455,
      "text": "That's the catalog \u2014 the things the store sells.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 111.455,
      "end": 114.135,
      "text": "A product id, and a product name.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 114.135,
      "end": 116.58,
      "text": "Different entity, so a different table.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 116.58,
      "end": 117.955,
      "text": "Users stay put.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 117.955,
      "end": 119.83,
      "text": "Products is its own box.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 119.83,
      "end": 122.302,
      "text": "Reviews live in a third table.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 122.302,
      "end": 125.955,
      "text": "A review has an id, some text, and a time.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 125.955,
      "end": 132.705,
      "text": "It also has two pointers, because a review is a relationship: someone wrote it, about a product.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 132.705,
      "end": 134.691,
      "text": "Look at reviews.email.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 134.691,
      "end": 137.496,
      "text": "That value matches users.email.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 137.496,
      "end": 139.094,
      "text": "That's who wrote the review.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 139.094,
      "end": 141.26,
      "text": "Same email, two tables.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 141.26,
      "end": 143.427,
      "text": "The relationship is the match.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 143.427,
      "end": 144.941,
      "text": "There's a second pointer.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 144.941,
      "end": 150.038,
      "text": "Reviews.product_id matches products.product_id.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 150.038,
      "end": 151.955,
      "text": "That's which item they reviewed.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 151.955,
      "end": 156.108,
      "text": "Two quiet matches, and you can ask who said what about which product.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 156.108,
      "end": 157.969,
      "text": "States is a tiny lookup.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 157.969,
      "end": 163.302,
      "text": "A state id and a name \u2014 so you don't spell California fifty different ways.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 163.302,
      "end": 165.33,
      "text": "Addresses hang off users.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 165.33,
      "end": 167.955,
      "text": "Street, city, postal code.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 167.955,
      "end": 172.83,
      "text": "Plus a user id that points back to users: whose place this is.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 172.83,
      "end": 175.469,
      "text": "And a state id that points at states.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-10-0098s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 175.469,
      "end": 178.177,
      "text": "Those matching fields light up the same way.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-11-0175s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 178.177,
      "end": 180.691,
      "text": "That's whose address, and which state.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-11-0175s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 180.691,
      "end": 182.385,
      "text": "The tables stay small.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-11-0175s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 182.385,
      "end": 186.941,
      "text": "Inside each table: rows, columns, and keys.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-11-0175s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 186.941,
      "end": 189.663,
      "text": "Between the tables: relationships.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-11-0175s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 189.663,
      "end": 192.552,
      "text": "That's what a relational database is made of.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-11-0175s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 192.552,
      "end": 195.705,
      "text": "Next we'll look inside one table: products.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-11-0175s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 195.756,
      "end": 201.922,
      "text": "A table looks a lot like a spreadsheet \u2014 with rows and columns \u2014 but it isn\u2019t a junk drawer.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-11-0175s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 201.922,
      "end": 208.964,
      "text": "One table has one job: it represents a single entity, or a single relationship between entities.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-12-0201s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 208.964,
      "end": 210.297,
      "text": "So what\u2019s an entity?",
      "slide": "slides/slide-13-0204s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 210.297,
      "end": 218.145,
      "text": "It\u2019s just a thing you can describe \u2014 a product, a customer, an order \u2014 something with attributes you care about.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-13-0204s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 218.145,
      "end": 221.756,
      "text": "Let\u2019s say you run an online store called the Sci-Fi Collective.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-13-0204s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 221.756,
      "end": 229.839,
      "text": "They sell weird gear, including a time machine that only takes you back five minutes \u2014 you know, in case you forgot your keys.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-13-0204s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 229.839,
      "end": 231.728,
      "text": "Each product is an entity.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-13-0204s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 231.728,
      "end": 236.561,
      "text": "It has a name, a description, a price, and a manufacturer.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-13-0204s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 236.561,
      "end": 241.103,
      "text": "Those become the columns in your table, and each product becomes a row.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-13-0204s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 241.103,
      "end": 245.381,
      "text": "And you\u2019ll almost always add one more column: a product ID.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-13-0204s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 245.381,
      "end": 252.228,
      "text": "It has to be unique \u2014 no doubles \u2014 so you can point at exactly one product and nowhere else.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-14-0242s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 252.228,
      "end": 258.381,
      "text": "That\u2019s your primary key: one per table, the \u201cthis row \u2014 and only this row\u201d handle.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-14-0242s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 258.381,
      "end": 260.339,
      "text": "Keep one entity per table.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-14-0242s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 260.339,
      "end": 263.45,
      "text": "Break that rule, and things get ugly fast.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-14-0242s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 263.45,
      "end": 267.589,
      "text": "What if you cram customers and products into one giant table?",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 267.589,
      "end": 271.075,
      "text": "You\u2019ll repeat the same customer info over and over.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 271.075,
      "end": 274.7,
      "text": "That\u2019s redundancy \u2014 and then the real problems show up.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 274.7,
      "end": 279.506,
      "text": "Here\u2019s a delete anomaly: that customer only lives in one row.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 279.506,
      "end": 283.103,
      "text": "Delete the product, and you\u2019ve just deleted the customer too.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 283.103,
      "end": 291.825,
      "text": "Here\u2019s an insertion anomaly: you want to add a product nobody\u2019s bought yet, but the table demands customer info on every row.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 291.825,
      "end": 294.867,
      "text": "So you\u2019re stuck \u2014 you can\u2019t even insert the product.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 294.867,
      "end": 295.936,
      "text": "One table.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 295.936,
      "end": 298.978,
      "text": "One entity \u2014 or one clear relationship.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 298.978,
      "end": 301.783,
      "text": "Hold that line, and your data stays clean.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 301.783,
      "end": 308.895,
      "text": "Now, the software that runs all of this is the RDBMS: the relational database management system.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 308.895,
      "end": 316.27,
      "text": "You\u2019ll hear names like MySQL, MariaDB, PostgreSQL, SQL Server, and SQLite.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 316.27,
      "end": 321.297,
      "text": "It talks to the hardware, stores the data, and gives you tools to work with it.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 321.297,
      "end": 324.908,
      "text": "The big one is SQL \u2014 Structured Query Language.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 324.908,
      "end": 329.214,
      "text": "That\u2019s how you create tables, change data, and ask questions.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 329.214,
      "end": 333.797,
      "text": "Vendors add their own flavors, but the core language travels well.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 333.797,
      "end": 336.408,
      "text": "Learn it once, and you can move around.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 336.408,
      "end": 341.131,
      "text": "You don\u2019t always have to write SQL by hand \u2014 some tools generate it for you.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 341.131,
      "end": 343.436,
      "text": "But knowing SQL makes you sharper.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 343.436,
      "end": 350.311,
      "text": "You\u2019ll catch integrity problems sooner, understand performance better, and scale with fewer surprises.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 350.311,
      "end": 351.853,
      "text": "Okay \u2014 first query.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 351.853,
      "end": 355.006,
      "text": "We\u2019re using the Sci-Fi Collective\u2019s product table.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-15-0262s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 355.006,
      "end": 359.283,
      "text": "The goal is to get the names of products that cost more than twenty bucks.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-16-0352s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 359.283,
      "end": 360.27,
      "text": "Here it is:",
      "slide": "slides/slide-16-0352s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 360.27,
      "end": 366.45,
      "text": "SELECT name FROM product WHERE price is greater than 20 \u2014 and finish with a semicolon.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-16-0352s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 366.45,
      "end": 367.242,
      "text": "Run it.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-16-0352s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 367.292,
      "end": 370.325,
      "text": "You should get one column with three product names.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-16-0352s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 370.386,
      "end": 372.344,
      "text": "That\u2019s your first SQL query.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-16-0352s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 372.344,
      "end": 378.108,
      "text": "Typo a column name \u2014 \u201cnames\u201d instead of \u201cname\u201d \u2014 and SQL will yell at you.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-16-0352s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 378.108,
      "end": 378.844,
      "text": "Good.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-16-0352s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 378.844,
      "end": 380.567,
      "text": "It\u2019s picky on purpose.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-16-0352s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 380.567,
      "end": 382.247,
      "text": "So what\u2019s actually happening?",
      "slide": "slides/slide-16-0352s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 382.247,
      "end": 385.289,
      "text": "SELECT picks the columns \u2014 we asked for name.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-16-0352s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 385.289,
      "end": 387.469,
      "text": "FROM picks the table \u2014 product.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-16-0352s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 387.469,
      "end": 391.025,
      "text": "WHERE filters the rows \u2014 only prices over twenty.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-16-0352s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 391.025,
      "end": 393.58,
      "text": "And the semicolon means we\u2019re done here.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-16-0352s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 393.58,
      "end": 399.692,
      "text": "SQL reads a bit like English\u2026 if English skipped the small talk and made you stick to the script.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-17-0393s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 399.692,
      "end": 401.344,
      "text": "Specific clauses.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-17-0393s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 401.344,
      "end": 402.692,
      "text": "Specific shape.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-17-0393s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 402.692,
      "end": 406.4,
      "text": "The database does exactly what you asked \u2014 nothing more.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-18-0402s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 406.505,
      "end": 407.649,
      "text": "Quick recap.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-18-0402s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 407.649,
      "end": 412.441,
      "text": "Spreadsheets break when life gets complicated, and structure matters.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-18-0402s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 412.441,
      "end": 420.816,
      "text": "Relational databases organize data into tables around entities, with primary keys to identify each row.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-18-0402s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 420.816,
      "end": 425.482,
      "text": "An RDBMS manages that world, and SQL is how you talk to it.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-18-0402s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 425.482,
      "end": 428.76,
      "text": "Those are the foundations \u2014 and they\u2019re just the start.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-20-0423s.png"
    },
    {
      "start": 428.76,
      "end": 435.343,
      "text": "Next time, we dig into the building blocks of SQL so you can read and write queries without guessing.",
      "slide": "slides/slide-20-0423s.png"
    }
  ]
}
